      "id": "v32z40q",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. INTRODUCTION TO DETERMINERS"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Determiners introduce nouns to specify quantity, possession, distance, or definiteness.",
        "'Few' and 'Little' express a negative sense (almost none), while 'A Few' and 'A Little' express a positive sense (some).",
        "'Each' highlights individual items within a definite set, whereas 'Every' addresses the group collectively.",
        "Uncountable nouns take quantifiers like 'Much' and 'Little', whereas countable nouns take 'Many' and 'Few'.",
        "Double determiners modifying a single noun represent a high-frequency error in competitive exams."
      ],
      "id": "aiszw56"
    },
